<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">As he walked out of the courtroom in the i=
nternational court of justice last week, a Rohingya civil society leader ca=
lled out to me, then threw a big two-handed thumbs up. He was beaming, as w=
ere all the Rohingya who listened as the <a href=3D"https://ablink.editoria=
l.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBMPiQ=
QXneH1j-HC6lHqbUOq1R_szSEdukb8lzMWPH6kUH3VRYcGhSI6vQ4pAoZLYunEflP_NoWDQg3Da=
uKWZyGLySvoSi46ZDONz273zQCWs6fPvI27ulACILbS_MhEUJyukF1teGVCchgQWQ6gGryY9sEq=
o_Mhdyk5qGWJJq4DTSaC8wBxj1-N8saojsN4U1nXvYQzu6qJJSvznVcyA1kzikrhtqmCDEpfRgT=
b4aPa10YEBsx9v3edxoO1uHn9sfeDhmtDNmmpiTfS_29iX-wnEoFAziDDu9Udm4XBJaBRQ/4w1/=
DbKeVyDdSD2rZ_dwNCl1MQ/h26/h001.9YOgqnBixSXxJi7izSWTxsWHNz4Zy0KOq4VdHO2LM2c=
" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">world=E2=80=99s top court recognised that they =
were survivors of genocide</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For more than a decade, I have written abo=
ut the ethnic minority long persecuted by Myanmar; last week was a rare mom=
ent when they had cause to celebrate. Decades of persecution have left the =
Rohingya stateless and seen them subjected to massacres, sexual violence, r=
ounded up and forced into camps and chased across the border as their villa=
ges are wiped off the map. Only a small fraction of them remain in their ho=
mes in Myanmar=E2=80=99s Rakhine state.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">For the Rohingya, the court=E2=80=99s ruli=
ng was the moment they were finally seen and heard. It was also recognition=
 of the work they have done in documenting their abuse, which was used in t=
he courts and has often featured in the Guardian, <a href=3D"https://ablink=
.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCS=
neHECPjjpeCiFtZxsMGbRZyz8cdbSTmp8cz1oTozKlVrgoncaiHj8TlRwq0mJK4jND7zOvgAZA2=
zLfv2Ql9uT5nG8FOeV_fZVP7_gpLJJRd1uBZpcf86kEYmtGc_Gvo_ExbHli_sIUC40S9iy3vgZX=
p0Utk4UIYBm_kC2AQd0rui9sHflbU-Z-Cve0aVgfRH2oRAWDtaBjlGlMSacOyT51RU0OSQrShrd=
Rdi6CLXtWBj3qFbUTuVZ5BuA10hZGOoXmMGhSlpfwKvoZU3V17rWND13Mayf4Oq1SNCqNUL2D1y=
3wikyjWPOkz0YCL1C_IDzkCQU/4w1/DbKeVyDdSD2rZ_dwNCl1MQ/h27/h001.SLtVEh7DaQPup=
1cmQfSoWdpzpevJPnhRJzXSr5GS4gA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">from places such =
as Tula Toli</a>, where hundreds were killed in a single day. They have bee=
n collected by people such as Yassin Abdumonab, a Rohingya journalist I hav=
e worked with since 2017, and has helped me report on <a href=3D"https://ab=
link.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgs=
zcCSneHEAiRBr1D54H8fToSvY8ifPi0Hi0pXg7AeOWV9BtD7Jw4tgPX6SARNA6vW51Y__Q2Iuxc=
Mhvj1Sz_55krfPAB3b4L7MVWwpC-3LIDx6-0BwBohf9c_IvyyNqF_kihwQpkJMLrq7rcTzBWaii=
C8GZbcuhknwDXenIb5d3SpKwfSKbCQNitxBqWHz7fMg2zbOGrM03arZyJKrSiTTezNrtwlCxRE2=
A4fwJyWE7HJKb-cP_XJneCI44HAJv4vXV6Anx3nDwTFjZHkX7mVqj79OBp7bfPrhPUVkZVwiA0n=
74eQ6qgTPC73GQ61kEIVRTozsaxT8/4w1/DbKeVyDdSD2rZ_dwNCl1MQ/h28/h001.n8hBwV6Cn=
Kv91CcC0wm0Tm-nn0oCwtg2Y8hwyrnVVA4" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Rohingya vict=
ims of human trafficking</a> and how the minority of Rohingya remaining in =
Myanmar are to this day being <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardi=
an.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECViDoBXM111GPfwX=
hNil2DjMu4MP8IFqbssk2W7uY19UPhLwp1R525FQBgAovdBulMZYTHdXFIqWwRZGqrDLcVq55FA=
DiuAQ5ChDcvxCmn0VIP8s_BMcXzlrpuS2UJCIhNexqEvX7sEvCgcGBn5GTjCBRhrEiqXUNNC1mG=
h6FLcv3vTjujm7XF35AK3hrenwVTmdw-N9tIpihJsKZPCwzBBIloYOol8GRJRSgGaoULAMh9Rc5=
TFv9Cw6n89BbOMNpi0E-EHTJFt8FN-77qXGIIGiPW7i0eBvFyr6s0o6mIhGrH1YMPR7j2WVHYzk=
yApGHgDATcismDqQmdrjhUtWqu/4w1/DbKeVyDdSD2rZ_dwNCl1MQ/h29/h001.BdXu0XjGpUoY=
otwcECV_IXHPGsezMuhnBEAjV95L-RA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">rounded into cam=
ps while their homes are destroyed</a>.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The testimony we hear from the people at t=
he heart of the crises we report on is where the power lies, whether it is =
the Rohingya or victims of <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.=
com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECViDoBXM111GPfwXhNi=
l2Dq1ARLPd_gi8NGsy9Nja2_pYxh87JbSS5BCmNBdsPajXGd3x5wxPjfs3D024YIg-KfbAC9EQo=
qAU6nUsB9O60U4zGbqTR1jvqAYwA79yxiFbnPc9sd8MgAFCjHDIJR-UtrkEK6HXK2i2AJjc8-KS=
CwwEjiuupRgGWPYLFUjVxJz5vj8wxkDWX3msTu7fc4u7z7RcWJPQTYzSYfvlFDGzHSRvL_tt8cn=
fH5-2Zvl5SQcnzJdosG1AQW8lKvAik8t7nYnP94j3c9X-hrYB7iwyVyD4_IhhrEgTVcztDGPSFf=
yCSnf5zjB3_aWpH_ZnGzZc9/4w1/DbKeVyDdSD2rZ_dwNCl1MQ/h30/h001.TZcnUGldWbzB5qB=
87txO0ojEbIy9YBWEklEHUknQXU0" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">drone strikes in So=
malia</a> or <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.=
Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECViDoBXM111GPfwXhNil2D7fA3QaxpGgZ=
pGxPAERAiJlmwKDPYIwxkajiT0pl6zvqLoUA7kae2WUtERug-NrjHbykcOF6wLzILKdTLo5bbTc=
gBXRhKCwf_d2eVSrxY8XLovefYVf2pDg3oOMiR0Jtj2YW0k4CRLS1YTKr6LykuMUicJDdsvDxdp=
KQBTcCzIWqIiRIA4IjH8Qbvvcf98uIJ7AoH0Uii3NxUm195PuMvw6NZLRHjy-qNZalT654wYt4K=
miEHirI_FIOK4znnP5nz7H26nNtg9-U22YuyHaGnsPMh0D0ZolC-tulDvsm4vi0/4w1/DbKeVyD=
dSD2rZ_dwNCl1MQ/h31/h001.nLYtVYuu5kjEkZIj35OBdtClntenYHV_sMBUIp8CsXY" style=
=3D"color: #0077B6;">massacres in Sudan</a>. Some of them, such as <a href=
=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18I=
RyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHECViDoBXM111GPfwXhNil2Dso1C3Kg_A6ALwAdWCIo8TVRHOXzclV6=
